  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Women, Girls, Boys and Men on ending Gender Based Violence in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a continuation of GHAB11 and will strengthen Civil Society Organisations&apos; (CSOs&apos;) institutional, technical and financial capacities so that they will be able to influence state and non -state actors to formulate and implement policies and services (including legal support, health, creation and expansion of safe spaces and holistic, gender -responsive access to justice) for survivors of Gender Based Violence (GBV). In addition, this project will target discriminatory social and gender norms that contribute to harmful attitudes and practices to prevent violence against women and girls by mobilising communities and influencing national and local stakeholders, including working with men and boys, through advocacy, and research and evidence -based campaigning and media.</narrative>
  </description>
